#
# Counter-example for math:StageIndexPresenceConstraint: a math:FiltrationStage that
# names its math:stageStructure but sits at NO index at all — it carries NEITHER a
# one-parameter math:filtrationThreshold NOR a multiparameter math:multiIndex. A stage
# must name its position in the filtration's index; one that names neither says nothing
# about WHERE it sits, so the cross-node disjunctive-existence constraint (a stage carries
# a threshold OR a multi-index) fires — shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent
# (math:UnderspecifiedFiltration).
# ISOLATION: the stage's own math:stageStructure frame IS satisfied (a math:TopologicalSpace
# is present), so the declarative missing-structure arm of math:UnderspecifiedFiltration
# stays silent; there is no second stage, so the monotonicity law is vacuous; and it is not
# a math:MultiparameterFiltration, so the collapse/diagonal guards cannot fire. EXACTLY ONE
# finding. Back-reference: math:StageIndexPresenceConstraint (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecStageNoIndex).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

# A stage naming its substructure but NEITHER a math:filtrationThreshold NOR a
# math:multiIndex — it sits at no index at all.
ex:stage a math:FiltrationStage ;
    math:stageStructure ex:cx .

ex:cx a math:TopologicalSpace .
